---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { url } from "../config/urls";
---
<DocsLayout title="5-minute guide" description="Install Virtual Me, run a browser task, create a recurring project, and find its results." path="guide/">
  <p class="eyebrow">About five minutes</p><h1>From a clean machine to useful browser work.</h1>
  <p class="lead">You need Node.js 22 or newer and a working Docker daemon. The first start downloads the bundled model, and CPU inference can take time; no fixed startup duration is promised.</p>
  <h2 id="check">1. Check the machine</h2><p>Confirm Node and Docker, then let the CLI inspect the setup.</p><CodeBlock code="node --version" /><CodeBlock code="docker info" /><CodeBlock code="npx virtualme doctor" />
  <h2 id="start">2. Start Virtual Me</h2><CodeBlock code="npx virtualme start" /><p>Wait for services to become healthy, then open <a href="http://localhost:8080">http://localhost:8080</a>. Keep the console on a trusted computer and private network: v1 has no authentication or TLS.</p>
  <h2 id="first-task">3. Ask one concrete task</h2><p>Open <strong>Chat</strong> and ask: “Visit the project repository, read the latest release notes, and summarize the operational changes with links.” Interactive chat starts work now and streams the agent's progress.</p>
  <h2 id="takeover">4. Watch and take over</h2><p>Open <strong>Desktop</strong>. It shows the real local Chromium window. You may use it directly whenever the agent is not actuating it; Jobs records the work.</p>
  <h2 id="project">5. Create recurring work</h2><p>Open <strong>Projects</strong>, create “Weekly project check,” enter a concrete browser task, choose a weekly selector, enable it, and save. Projects are scheduled independently from interactive chat and own a scratch directory.</p>
  <h2 id="results">6. Find the result</h2><p><strong>Jobs</strong> shows queue and activity history. <strong>Data</strong> browses artifacts under the mounted data directory, including project files and agent screenshots.</p>
  <h2 id="persistence">7. Keep, stop, and update</h2><p>The default host directory is <code>~/.virtualme</code>. It survives container replacement and holds Valkey state, Chromium profile, metrics, projects, agent artifacts, speech cache, and mail state.</p><CodeBlock code="npx virtualme stop" /><CodeBlock code="npx virtualme update" />
  <p>If health stays red, run <code>npx virtualme status</code> and <code>npx virtualme logs -f</code>. Continue with <a href={url("architecture/")}>how it works</a> or the current <a href="https://github.com/mayanklahiri/virtualme#readme">README troubleshooting guide</a>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
